nd questions ordinary eating with a cloth.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Sukkah 26b:9:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Sukkah_26b.9.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Sukkah 27a:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Sukkah_27a.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3018:3:link-003","he":[243,259],"en":[433,443],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yoma_79a.3.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Yoma 79a:3:1","assessment":"Both sides of the folio discuss this tradition. Their distinction between food categories belongs to the commentary.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Yoma 79a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yoma_79a.3.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Yoma 79b:1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yoma_79b.1.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3018:3:link-004","he":[260,276],"en":[445,471],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yevamot_15b.2.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Yevamot 15b:2:1","assessment":"The gloss takes his status as a given in the olive incident and discusses his school.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Yevamot 15b:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yevamot_15b.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3018:3:link-005","he":[277,293],"en":[473,493],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin_107a.12.2"},"reference":"Tosafot on Chullin 107a:12:2","assessment":"Tosafot draws on parallel arguments, but its Berakhot page label also varies. Preserve the text and link the actual Tosafot target.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Chullin 107a:12:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin_107a.12.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Berakhot 19b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_19b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3018:3:link-006","he":[310,331],"en":[526,545],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_19b.6"},"reference":"Berakhot 19b:6","assessment":"The speaker is Elazar son of Tzadok. Tosafot infers priesthood from the avoidance of impurity; Yuhasin offers competing readings.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 19b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_19b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Sukkah 26b:9:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Sukkah_26b.9.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource Hebrew transcription"}]},{"id":"3018:3:link-007","he":[332,361],"en":[547,581],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot_36a.12"},"reference":"Bekhorot 36a:12","assessment":"The firstborn episode is the locus used for the inference. Ownership is explicit, while its bearing on the question remains debated by Yuhasin.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bekhorot 36a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot_36a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource Hebrew transcription"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"holds":[{"raw":"וספק אם היה כהן","reason":"Multiple text-specific evidence lines remain in tension. Avot De-Rabbi Natan has his self-description, Tosafot takes priesthood as given, and Yuhasin argues that the inference is open to objections.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avot DeRabbi Natan 16:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avot_DeRabbi_Natan_16.2"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Tosafot on Sukkah 26b:9:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Sukkah_26b.9.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource Hebrew transcription"}]},{"raw":"שנשבה ר\"צ לרומי","reason":"Rome is in Heilprin’s telling. The located Avot De-Rabbi Natan narrative does not specify the location.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avot DeRabbi Natan 16:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avot_DeRabbi_Natan_16.2"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."}]},{"raw":"במנורת המאור הלכות ותשובה","reason":"The cited edition is expressly distinguished from Aboab. A bounded check of Al-Nakawa’s digital Laws of Repentance found no exact Tzadok passage. The precise parallel remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avot DeRabbi Natan 16:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avot_DeRabbi_Natan_16.2"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, First Treatise, Fourth Millennium","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_ראשון/האלף_הרביעי"},"witness":"Wikisource Hebrew transcription"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Elazar is expressly ben Tzadok in the coffin and olive traditions. This establishes the patronymic used there.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The story includes captivity, the matron, the enslaved woman and his statement of priestly descent. This digital passage does not specify Rome.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Yuhasin explicitly proposes this explanation. Keep the motive conjectural.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The first gloss cites the two proof passages. The second assumes the same status and questions ordinary eating with a cloth.","