get":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_39b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 56a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_56a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"בתוספתא דכלאים אמר על הטוהר הזה ישב חגי הנביא","reason":"The exact claimed wording in Tosefta Kilayim was not located in the received digital collection. Yevamot has a similar expression about a mortar in the mouth of Dosa, which does not establish Tzadok’s claim.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 16a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_16a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"וכ\"כ ר' דוראן בפירוש הפרקים","reason":"Magen Avot on the cited Avot paragraph discusses Tzadok’s relationship to the Temple and later figures. The exact four-hundred-year assertion still needs an identified passage.","evidence":[{"reference":"Magen Avot on Avot 4:5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Magen_Avot_on_Avot_4.5.1"},"witness":"Magen Avot, Leipzig 1855"},{"reference":"Yevamot 16a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_16a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"עם ר' דוסא בן הרכינס","reason":"Dosa is directly present in the parallel Haggai report in Yevamot and in Yuhasin’s own chronology. A direct co-occurrence for Tzadok and Dosa as asserted here remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 16a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_16a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The fasting is stated to last forty years, with Jerusalem as the object of preservation. Keep Heilprin’s Temple wording as his summary.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Yoma connects the opening doors with Yohanan ben Zakkai’s rebuke and quotes Zechariah.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The corresponding Sanhedrin text gives the relocation of the court and cessation of capital cases. It does not narrate the doors.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The baraita explicitly dates the court’s move forty years before the destruction.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The midrash names Vespasian, the retrieval of Tzadok, his restoration and Elazar’s proposal to reward the doctors by teaching them. The Bavli version explicitly gives the request for physicians.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Both relevant accounts make Tzadok the patient. Identify the referent to avoid reading the pronoun as Yohanan ben Zakkai.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The midrash gives instruction in finger reckoning plus another item. Keep Heilprin’s excerpt and attach the midrash’s order of events.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The gloss expressly explains finger reckoning as multiplication on the fingers.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The age is the entry’s explicit inference held with the underlying unresolved Haggai attribution.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The midrash explicitly names the two children of Tzadok the priest.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Gittin presents a recognizably parallel captivity story with Yishmael ben Elisha as father. The two source traditions and the entry’s choice are kept distinct.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Yuhasin explicitly distinguishes the possible identities. No consolidation is made.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The oven story follows the exposition that applies the verse to Tzadok and his peers.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The internal notice quotes Gilgulei Neshamot and reports an identification attributed to Yuhasin. Preserve the distinct mystical and biographical voices.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"This is a mystical identification in the internal source, not a historical equivalence.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The doors and prophecy are direct in Yoma. The exact Yuhasin sentence linking that event to Tzadok’s foreknowledge remains open in the checked digital transcription.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The exact claimed wording in Tosefta Kilayim was not located in the received digital collection. Yevamot has a similar expression about a mortar in the mouth of Dosa, which does not establish Tzadok’s claim.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Magen Avot on the cited Avot paragraph discusses Tzadok’s relationship to the Temple and later figures. The exact four-hundred-year assertion still needs an identified passage.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Dosa is directly present in the parallel Haggai report in Yevamot and in Yuhasin’s own chronology. A direct co-occurrence for Tzadok and Dosa as asserted here remains open.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 56a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_56a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 39b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_39b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zechariah 11:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zechariah_11.1"},"witness":"Miqra according to the Masorah"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 41a:25","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_41a.25"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 8b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_8b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:31","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eikhah_Rabbah_1.31"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Gittin 56b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_56b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yefeh Anaf on Eichah Rabbah 1:31","target":{"url":"https://or-breslev.co.il/library/יפה-ענף-על-איכה-רבה/פרשה-א/פסקה-לא/"},"witness":"Or Breslev Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:46","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/E